# OpenAI gpt-oss-120b (2025): 36 layers of GQA, every other one in a 128-token sliding
# window and the rest global, each head with a learned sink logit. Every layer's MoE
# has 128 experts of 2880, 4 a token. Attention's projections have biases, and YaRN
# stretches RoPE 32x from 4096.
#
# The experts here are a SwiGLU clamped at 7, which costs what gpt-oss's
# gate * sigmoid(1.702 gate) * (up + 1) does, and they and the router have no biases.
d_model    = 2880
vocab_size = 201088

norm    = rmsnorm(eps=1e-5)
attn    = gqa(num_heads=64, num_kv_heads=8, head_dim=64, bias=true, sinks=true,
              rope=rope(base=150000, scaling=yarn(factor=32, original_max_len=4096)))
local   = attn(sliding_window_size=128)
experts = moe(num_experts=128, top_k=4,
              expert=gated_mlp(intermediate_size=2880, activation=swish, limit=7.0))

L = [norm local] [norm experts]
G = [norm attn] [norm experts]

model = embed "LG"^18 norm head
